00:10:05,281 --> 00:10:08,360
The shark is coming straight towards me.

264
00:10:08,361 --> 00:10:10,900
- It's right under you, Kathy.

265
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:14,080
(upbeat music)

266
00:10:14,081 --> 00:10:16,520
- All right, well, Marco, I was telling you

267
00:10:16,521 --> 00:10:20,600
that I used to spend
every summer on the lake,

268
00:10:20,601 --> 00:10:24,874
and my family had a
really small house on a small

269
00:10:24,954 --> 00:10:29,480
island, and my cousins
had another small house

270
00:10:29,481 --> 00:10:34,160
on another small island, so
our families are really close,

271
00:10:34,161 --> 00:10:37,160
and we used to go to one
house for dinner one night,

272
00:10:37,161 --> 00:10:40,080
and the other house
didn't earth the next night.

273
00:10:40,081 --> 00:10:42,640
So everyone was over at my cousin's house,

274
00:10:42,641 --> 00:10:47,480
except for my grandfather,
and so he was thinking,

275
00:10:47,481 --> 00:10:50,760
"Okay, it's late, maybe I
better go pick up my wife

276
00:10:50,761 --> 00:10:55,040
and see what's going on,"
so he goes into the boat.

277
00:10:55,041 --> 00:10:58,480
It's dark, there's no light on the boat.

278
00:10:58,481 --> 00:11:03,557
He's driving straight towards
the island, when suddenly my

279
00:11:03,558 --> 00:11:08,080
cousin, in his boat, drives
directly into my grandfather.

280
00:11:08,081 --> 00:11:09,880
- So they crashed, they crashed.

281
00:11:09,881 --> 00:11:11,520
- Two boats crashed in the lake.

282
00:11:11,521 --> 00:11:15,000
- And then my grandfather's
boat flipped over,

283
00:11:15,001 --> 00:11:18,960
turned upside down,
and he fell in the water.

284
00:11:18,961 --> 00:11:20,040
- But he was okay, right?

285
00:11:20,041 --> 00:11:24,800
- Yeah, he was okay, but he
was really angry about this,

286
00:11:24,801 --> 00:11:31,520
and the boat stayed in the water,
and the engine fell down to the bottom.

287
00:11:31,521 --> 00:11:34,360
So we had to go the next
morning to get the boat,

288
00:11:34,361 --> 00:11:37,400
and we actually had to
hire some scuba divers

289
00:11:37,401 --> 00:11:40,600
to go to the bottom of
the lake to get the engine.

290
00:11:40,601 --> 00:11:41,565
- Wow.

291
00:11:41,589 --> 00:11:42,280
- Yeah.

292
00:11:42,281 --> 00:11:44,800
- I imagine your grandpa was pretty angry.

293
00:11:44,801 --> 00:11:47,680
- Yeah, he tells the story every year.

294
00:11:47,681 --> 00:11:50,320
- Exactly, but you know what?

295
00:11:50,321 --> 00:11:53,920
I've got a million of
these crazy lake stories,

296
00:11:54,369 --> 00:11:56,640
'cause my family--
- It always happens.

297
00:11:56,641 --> 00:11:58,000
- Yeah.

298
00:11:58,001 --> 00:12:00,360
- All right, guys, well, do
